  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader using the Legacy theme in dark mode, I want the **standard** dark style to sit on a light grey, as the legacy app did, not on pure black. Only the « plus sombre » and « OLED » styles go to (near) black. I also want **no alternating tint between messages**, which does not help readability. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-18.)\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n- `ThemeAppearance.readerDarkSurfaces` (`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/ThemeAppearance.swift:73-81`) gives the reader background as follows:\n  - `.standard`: `0x000000`, pure black, the same as OLED;\n  - `.darker`: `0x0B0B0C`;\n  - `.oled`: `0x000000`.\n\n  The reader CSS falls back to `#000000` too (`reader.css:42`). The web view's own layer uses the same value (`readerBackground`, `:177-184`).\n- Alternation: even messages sit on `--surface-alt` (`reader.css:19-25, 103-104`, #568), with even-message variants for the classic header and the quote tints (`reader.css:261-286`).\n\n### Legacy reference (@ 87fe0d1c)\n\n- The dark reader page is grey: `body.ios7 { background: rgba(46, 47, 51, 1) }` and `.message .content { background: rgba(46, 47, 51, 1) }`, i.e. #2E2F33 (`SuperHFRplus/Assets/HTML/style-liste-dark.css:263-266, 563-564`).\n- There is no alternating message background in legacy's dark CSS: #568 is a SwiftHFR addition.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. **Standard dark style = legacy grey.** The `.standard` page background becomes the legacy #2E2F33.\n   - Its quote, placeholder and separator surfaces are re-derived so they stay distinct from the page and keep every contrast pair (`ThemeDefinitionTests`, the reader contrast tests): text #F2F2F7 and secondary #A1A1A6 on #2E2F33, links, the accent.\n   - « Plus sombre » (#0B0B0C) and « OLED » (#000000) are unchanged.\n   - The brightness slider still applies on top.\n2. **App screens in the standard dark style**: check what the list and screen backgrounds are in dark mode for the Legacy theme, and say in the PR whether they follow the same grey. Legacy's dark list rows: `style-liste-dark.css:330` `rgba(38, 40, 47, 1)` and `:502`. Cite what legacy's native screens used (`AppThemePalette`, `Common.swift:813-835` @ 87fe0d1c) before changing anything native. If native screens need a change, describe it and do it in the same PR only if it is small; otherwise open a follow-up.\n3. **Remove the alternating message tint** (#568) for every theme and style:\n   - drop `--surface-alt` and its even-message rules, including the classic-header and quote-tint variants written for even messages;\n   - keep the message separator rule (`--separator-strong`).\n\n   Record it as a `gap-edit` (#568's row): a deliberate return to legacy.\n4. Settings preview and the theme gallery follow (they read `readerSurfaces`).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test pins the standard background at #2E2F33, and darker/OLED unchanged. It fails on today's code.\n- [ ] The contrast tests pass on the new surfaces.\n- [ ] No message has a different background from its neighbour. A reader-HTML test pins it.\n- [ ] Before/after screenshots (Legacy theme, dark, standard / plus sombre / OLED), plus a device check on the next general review (#893).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
