   "body": "·/·r·elease cloud/i1038-sonnet\n\nHand-off (operator asked to write everything down; the orchestrator lost the link). **Where it stands: PR #1212, ready, approved, waiting on CI and the merge.**\n\n- **PR:** #1212, head `9781964f74d8b4fe275b8218c36611c54f301f6f`, not a draft, `compile-check` label on. Opus 5.5 verdicts are posted on the PR: round 3 APPROVE on `2dd96b23`, delta round 4 APPROVE on `9781964f` (a CI fix to `ReaderThemeTests.aThemeRecoloursThePageAndLegacyRestoresIt`, which still expected the old black page). Ready line posted on #893.\n- **CI at the time of writing:** every check green on `9781964f` except « App build + tests (iOS 27 simulator) », still running (that is the run that decides whether the one failing test is fixed; I never saw its log, and nothing has been run locally: Linux, no Xcode).\n- **What is left, for whoever picks it up:**\n  1. Wait for « App build + tests » on `9781964f`; if it is red, read its log (`gh api repos/ezzz/HFRnow/actions/jobs/<id>/logs`) and fix the test, not the page.\n  2. Merge #1212 (squash; auto-merge was enabled by the operator).\n  3. Close this issue with `Done in #1212 (merged as <sha>)`: merges into `dev-swift` do not close issues.\n  4. Optional doc edits carried in the PR body (not pushed, to keep the APPROVE): `docs/lots/LOT-122-appearance.md:31` still says « the alternate message surface and the 1 px rule follow the style »; the legacy line order in the `ThemeAppearanceTests` doc comment (`body.ios7` is `:563-564`, `.message .content` `:262-266`); « stay derived » → « stays derived » in `LOT-188:51`.\n  5. Device check and before/after screenshots (Legacy theme, dark: standard, plus sombre, OLED) on #893.\n- **Follow-ups opened from this work:** #1215 (dead `readerAlternate` contrast pair in `HFRModels`), #1216 (night accent and links under 4.5:1 on the grey for 161 of 360 hues; same as legacy).\n- **Stacked on this PR:** #1219 (#1213), branched from `fix/1210-dark-grey`; after #1212 merges, retarget it to `dev-swift` and merge `dev-swift` into it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
